[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   Step 124 -- lineage-independent aphelion dipole (SBDB eras).
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   The prospective analysis (step_117) found that the post-2017 SBDB
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   cohort fails the registered three-leg residual test, and the
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   factorial audit (steps_118-120) diagnosed a unipolar,
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   cohort-private residual field pointing ~(120, -40) that is
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   invisible to the CODE machinery at the same sky.  The residual
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   channel is reconstruction machinery; the aphelion-direction
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   channel is not -- each comet's aphelion unit vector is a function
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   of the published osculating elements (w, Om, i) alone, with no
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   three-leg integration and no catalogue boundary solution.  The
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   residual failure therefore does not automatically doom the
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   spatial datum: if the newly designated population leans toward
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   the declared axis in its aphelia, the sky anomaly exists in an
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   independently discovered, independently fitted population and
[2026-09-21 15:14:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 124]   the caveat narrows to the reconstruction channel.
